FADE IN:

EXT. CITY STREET — STREET — DUSK

A street of brownstones and glass towers at dusk. Copper light on the stoops. Windows come on one by one, like a city putting on its earrings.

[[TIME: 5]]
[[MUSIC: Main title cue: a big band warming up somewhere out of sight. Music only; no dialogue in this release.]]
[[SFX: Street bed: a bus sighing, a door, distant laughter.]]

EXT. CITY STREET — TAILOR'S SHOPFRONT — DUSK

[[ENTER: TAILOR]]

A tailor in shirtsleeves lowers the grille on his shop. Halfway down he stops, ducks under, and straightens the lapel on the mannequin in the window. Then he locks up and pats the glass goodnight.

[[TIME: 5]]
[[EXIT: TAILOR]]

EXT. CITY STREET — BUS STOP — DUSK

[[ENTER: TEENAGER]]

A teenager at the bus stop practises a dance step in the reflection of the shelter glass. Wrong. Wrong. Right. Nobody is watching, so he does it again for the pleasure of it.

[[TIME: 5]]

EXT. CITY STREET — FIRE ESCAPE — DUSK

[[ENTER: GRANDMOTHER]]

A grandmother hangs a jewel-green dress on her fire escape to air. She smooths the skirt with both hands and gives it a long look, as if the dress has a date tonight and she approves of him.

[[TIME: 5]]

EXT. CITY STREET — BALCONY KITCHEN — DUSK

[[ENTER: WOMAN ON THE BALCONY]]

Through an open balcony door, a woman dances alone in her kitchen. A wooden spoon for a partner. Completely unembarrassed.

[[TIME: 5]]

EXT. CITY STREET — NEIGHBOUR'S WINDOW — DUSK

[[ENTER: NEIGHBOUR]]
[[ENTER: WOMAN ON THE BALCONY]]

Across the street, her neighbour lifts his phone toward her balcony.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[PROP: PR-NEIGHBOUR-PHONE: raised toward the balcony]]
[[VFX: The lens blooms copper: the Ember, the city's everyday no.]]
[[INSERT: The phone's lens glowing copper.]]

He lowers the phone, embarrassed.

[[PROP: PR-NEIGHBOUR-PHONE: lowered]]

On her balcony, the woman has seen all of it. She raises her glass to him across the street, and keeps dancing.

[[TIME: 4]]

EXT. CITY STREET — ROOFTOPS — DUSK

[[SHOT: WIDE — RISING CRANE]]

The camera rises over water towers and fire escapes, over the green dress and the woman's lit kitchen, toward a ballroom glowing like a jewellery box across the rooftops: Halcyon House.

[[TIME: 6]]
[[MUSIC: The band lands its first full chord as the ballroom comes into view.]]

CUT TO BLACK.
